  "claim": "End to end, Theorem 4 of ticket B runs: for two positive NAE-3SAT formulas whose graphs G_k are non-planar with a one-crossing drawing, (a, a, b) with 2 solutions and (b, a, c)(c, b, c) with 4, the count is recovered exactly from the counts of instances built by ticket A at the crossing (k-snakes with k_S = 1, 3, 5, 7) over D + 1 values of k. Every one of the 44 instances is certified Pfaffian (planar pieces, glued Kasteleyn signing non-colourable), is non-planar, and has three twisted branches at every junction with no good root; the four counts per k give 9 #col(G_k), equal to the direct count.",
